From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dpnet: Peer, Client, Server and lobby objects keep session state (host, connect, application description, player info, groups, async operations, caps, registered programs)

The DirectPlay8 Peer, Client and Server objects were FIXME stubs that returned
fixed codes whatever their state. They now share one session object
(session.c) that keeps what an initialized object holds and answers the way
DirectPlay8 does for that state. There is no network engine: nothing answers
on a host address and a host has no remote players.

- Close: UNINITIALIZED when not initialized, cancels outstanding operations
  (USERCANCEL completions) and destroys the groups and players with
  DESTROY_GROUP / DESTROY_PLAYER messages, then the object is uninitialized.
- Host: validates the application description (size, flags, password,
  reserved data), device addresses and flags, keeps a copy with a new
  instance GUID, creates the local (host) player and sends CREATE_PLAYER
  with the player context; HOSTING / ALREADYCONNECTED / CONNECTING when the
  state forbids it. A server's own player is not a client: it is not
  listed, has no info, context or address through the client calls.
- Connect: parameter checks (INVALIDHOSTADDRESS, INCOMPLETEADDRESS, ...),
  then no host answers: a synchronous call returns NORESPONSE, an
  asynchronous one a handle and a CONNECT_COMPLETE with NORESPONSE after the
  connect time-out (cancellable with USERCANCEL).
- EnumHosts returns async handles; CancelAsyncOperation cancels by handle
  (INVALIDHANDLE otherwise, per object) or by DPNCANCEL_* flags and sends the
  USERCANCEL completion.
- Get/SetApplicationDesc (BUFFERTOOSMALL protocol, NOCONNECTION, NOTHOST),
  Set*Info / Get*Info for the local player, groups (create, destroy, add and
  remove members, info, contexts, enumerations, with their messages and
  async completions), player contexts, GetLocalHostAddresses / peer address,
  send queue info (empty), DestroyPeer / DestroyClient / TerminateSession
  state checks, loopback sends of a peer to itself or a group it is in
  (RECEIVE and SEND_COMPLETE, NOLOOPBACK honoured), ReturnBuffer
  (INVALIDHANDLE: no buffer is ever lent), connection info (INVALIDPLAYER:
  no remote players), GetCaps / SetCaps (DPN_CAPS and DPN_CAPS_EX, defaults
  200 ms / 14 retries / 60 s keep-alive), SP caps for the server,
  RegisterLobby (flags, NOTREGISTERED, ALREADYREGISTERED, INVALIDHANDLE).
- IDirectPlay8LobbiedApplication: RegisterProgram / UnRegisterProgram keep
  the program under HKLM\Software\Microsoft\DirectPlay8\Applications,
  SetAppAvailable, Close; the connection calls answer INVALIDHANDLE (no lobby
  client is connected).
- IDirectPlay8LobbyClient: EnumLocalPrograms lists the registered programs
  (DPL_APPLICATION_INFO + names, size protocol), ConnectApplication answers
  INVALIDAPPLICATION for an unregistered GUID and CANTLAUNCHAPPLICATION for a
  registered one (programs are not launched), Close succeeds, the connection
  calls answer INVALIDHANDLE.

The conformance tests' todo_wine marks that now pass are removed (client.c,
server.c).

